whether obstructive or non-obstructive. This process can be modified by lifestyle adjustments, pharmacological therapies, and invasive&#13;
interventions designed to achieve disease stabilization or regression.&#13;
The disease can have long, stable periods but can also become unstable at any time, typically due to an acute atherothrombotic event&#13;
caused by plaque rupture or erosion. However, the disease is&#13;
